Command	Description
kubectl version	            Shows the kubectl and cluster version
kubectl config view	            Displays kubeconfig settings
kubectl get nodes	            Lists all nodes in the cluster
kubectl get pods	            Lists all pods in the current namespace
kubectl get all	            Lists all resources in the current namespace
kubectl get services	L           ists all services
kubectl describe pod pod_name           	Shows detailed info about a pod
kubectl logs pod_name           	Shows logs from a container inside the pod
kubectl exec -it pod_name -- bash	            Access shell inside a running pod
kubectl create -f file.yaml         	Creates resource(s) from a YAML file
kubectl apply -f file.yaml	            Creates or updates resource(s) from a YAML file
kubectl delete -f file.yaml	            Deletes resource(s) defined in the YAML
kubectl delete pod pod_name	            Deletes a specific pod
kubectl get deployments	            Lists all deployments
kubectl rollout status deployment deployment_name	        Checks rollout status of a deployment
kubectl scale deployment deployment_name --replicas=3	            Scales deployment to 3 pods
kubectl expose deployment deployment_name --type=NodePort --port=80	            Exposes deployment as a service
kubectl port-forward pod/pod_name 8080:80	            Forwards local port to a pod port
kubectl config use-context context_name	            Switches to another kubeconfig context